  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Labor Integration of Migrant Women Heads of Household</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Concurrently, women face inherent structural challenges in accessing better job opportunities within the country, theme prominently addressed in the UN Women-funded project executed by IOM to empower and support women entrepreneurs. This project will continue the work with migrants, community groups and enterprises, aiming to identify the specific needs of companies to develop three customized courses adapted to promote job placement and address existing skills gaps. By adjusting these courses to the demands of available jobs, the project aims not only to equip migrant women with the necessary skills, but also help to fill vacancies in the labour market. The initiative is designed to cultivate meaningful connections between migrant workers and businesses eager to employ skilled personnel, encouraging a collaborative environment that supports the economic empowerment of migrant women.</narrative>
  </description>
